WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.497
A practical sensitive data protection baseline starts with identification.

2
00:00:05.497 --> 00:00:16.325
Know what sensitive data the C# application handles, classify it, minimize collection and copying, and map where it enters, flows, persists, and leaves.

3
00:00:16.325 --> 00:00:23.655
Keep secrets out of code, logs, client assets, public configuration, CI output, and support artifacts.

4
00:00:23.655 --> 00:00:26.404
Use appropriate TLS, encryption, ASP.

5
00:00:26.404 --> 00:00:34.566
NET Core Data Protection, password hashing, and key management based on the workflow and security property needed.

6
00:00:34.566 --> 00:00:41.146
Control storage across databases, files, caches, queues, backups, exports, and analytics.

7
00:00:41.146 --> 00:00:45.477
Redact logs, telemetry, exceptions, and support materials.

8
00:00:45.477 --> 00:00:51.974
Use DTOs and response shaping to prevent accidental overexposure through APIs and clients.

9
00:00:51.974 --> 00:01:02.552
Finally, enforce authorization and tenant boundaries on the server, use safe test data, define retention intentionally, and prepare for incidents.

10
00:01:02.552 --> 00:01:05.801
Sensitive data protection is not one feature.

11
00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:13.380
It is a set of design and operational habits that keep data exposure limited, explainable, and recoverable.
